    "b-engine-model-reducer-decision-22": {
      "id": "b-engine-model-reducer-decision-22",
      "type": "decision",
      "props": {
        "status": "accepted",
        "title": "Single reducer as mutation authority"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "reduceInteractiveCanvasState",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas/src/state/actions/reducer.ts",
              "symbol": "reduceInteractiveCanvasState"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the one function that turns "
        },
        {
          "insert": "(InteractiveCanvasState, CanvasAction)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " into a new state, and it is the only place a document is ever mutated. Interactive UI gestures dispatch the exact same "
        },
        {
          "insert": "CanvasAction",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " values an external agent or automation script would dispatch to make the identical change; neither path has a shortcut around the other. This choke point guarantees two properties regardless of an action's origin: consistent undo (every mutation goes through the same history bookkeeping, so a human edit and an agent edit undo identically) and waypoint coherence (every action that can move or resize an object flows through the same reconciliation pass). Splitting the reducer, or giving any caller a way to patch the document directly, would let those guarantees diverge quietly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-engine-model-waypoint-choke-23": {
      "id": "b-engine-model-waypoint-choke-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The reducer wraps the action switch with a stale-waypoint choke point: after any document-changing action (excluding undo/redo/reset), "
        },
        {
          "insert": "reconcileConnectionWaypoints",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas/src/state/actions/waypoints.ts",
              "symbol": "reconcileConnectionWaypoints"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " compares each waypointed connection's two endpoint owners before and after. If both owners translated by the same delta with no resize — a multi-select drag, a nudge, a section carrying its members — every waypoint shifts by that delta, preserving trunk-and-branch fan shapes. If the owners moved asymmetrically or either resized, the waypoints are dropped so the connector falls back to obstacle-avoiding auto-routing. Because this runs inside the reducer, the waypoint change shares the triggering action's history entry: one undo restores geometry and waypoints together."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
